    <briefdescription>
<para>Data <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_dependence" kindref="compound">Dependence</ref> Graph <ref refid="class_node" kindref="compound">Node</ref> The graph can represent the following types of nodes: </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Single instruction node containing just one instruction.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Multiple instruction node where two or more instructions from the same basic block are merged into one node.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Pi-block node which is a group of other DDG nodes that are part of a strongly-connected component of the graph. A pi-block node contains more than one single or multiple instruction nodes. The root node cannot be part of a pi-block.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Root node is a special node that connects to all components such that there is always a path from it to any node in the graph. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
